31:["$","ul",null,{"className":"tagged-list","children":[["$","li","Look for the Kobe stamp",{"className":"tagged-list__item--illustrated","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"tagged-list__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","svg",null,{"className":"guide-icon","data-guide-icon":"beef","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","aria-hidden":"true","focusable":"false","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.7","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","children":"$13:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:children:props:children"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__body","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__heading","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Look for the Kobe stamp"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Kobe is a specific wagyu from a specific breed, not a synonym for all Japanese beef. It is pricey and the best steak either of us has had. Omi and Matsusaka are other premium types—we have tried all three and found them fairly indistinguishable—but Kobe is easiest on a tourist route. Teppanyaki is ideal. Look for the official stamp: a small golden cow statue proving legitimacy."}],null]}]]}],["$","li","Take Japanese fruit seriously",{"className":"tagged-list__item--illustrated","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"tagged-list__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","svg",null,{"className":"guide-icon","data-guide-icon":"fruit","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","aria-hidden":"true","focusable":"false","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.7","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","children":"$13:props:children:2:props:children:4:props:children:0:props:children:props:children"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__body","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__heading","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Take Japanese fruit seriously"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Fruit is sold in grades; the top ones are pricey and worth trying once. Find beautifully packed fruit in supermarkets, department-store basements, and stations. Premium strawberries arrive toward winter at roughly ¥1,000–1,500 for six (about $10). We can barely eat strawberries at home now. Also try Shine Muscat grapes, muskmelon, apples, and mikan."}],null]}]]}],["$","li","Try kakigori",{"className":"tagged-list__item--illustrated","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"tagged-list__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","svg",null,{"className":"guide-icon","data-guide-icon":"kakigori","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","aria-hidden":"true","focusable":"false","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.7","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","children":"$2d:props:children:0:props:children:props:children"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__body","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__heading","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Try kakigori"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Japanese shaved ice is way better than versions we have tried elsewhere. It comes in every flavor; green tea is the classic."}],null]}]]}],["$","li","Explore Japanese whisky by the pour",{"className":"tagged-list__item--illustrated","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"tagged-list__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","svg",null,{"className":"guide-icon","data-guide-icon":"whisky","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","aria-hidden":"true","focusable":"false","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.7","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","children":"$2e:props:children:0:props:children:props:children"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__body","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"tagged-list__heading","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Explore Japanese whisky by the pour"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Bottles can oddly cost more in Japan than in the US, but bar and restaurant pours are much cheaper. Try Yamazaki, Hakushu, and Hibiki. Distillery tours use a lottery that